MAJOR_VERSION=4
STANDARD_VERSION=2
RELEASE_VERSION=0
PRERELEASE=1
DEV_VERSION=14
DESCRIPTION<<VER_END
PRE 4.2.0: Wi-Fi scan/join, WSL LAN server hosting, P3-13 multi-device server

Wi-Fi and platform
- lab scan/join: FL_NET_WIFI_HOME_SSID in scan; join by SSID without prior scan match;
  interactive password prompt; saved-network skip via fl_wifi.db; native Linux wpa_cli/nmcli
  (select_network, longer timeout, Pi-friendly errors)
- fl_platform WSL/Linux/macOS detection (fl_platform.c)
- FlinstonePowershell.exe (make flinstone-ps-windows): WlanAPI wifi-scan/join/leave/status,
  auto-discover under tools/; FlinstoneLinuxNet ELF helper with the same protocol
- WSL Wi-Fi backend routes through FlinstonePowershell; Windows Wi-Fi IP for LAN hints;
  network_bridge.py discover/relay fallback; tools/fl-wifi.env from install_deps

WSL LAN server (portproxy + firewall)
- server host on WSL: parameter-driven Windows netsh portproxy
  (listenaddress=<local-ip> → connectaddress=<wsl-ip>) plus inbound firewall rule
  "Flinstone Server <port>"; UAC elevation via FlinstonePowershell server-proxy; yellow
  NOTICE printed in the terminal before the UAC prompt; server kill / leave / exit remove
  both rules (server-proxy-del); server join unchanged; userspace server-bridge remains a
  non-admin fallback when portproxy is declined
- server host binds in WSL (0.0.0.0 when user passes Windows Wi-Fi IP); peers use the
  router-assigned Windows address (e.g. 192.168.1.x), not the internal 172.x eth0 NAT

Interactive shell
- Ctrl+C (^C) at the prompt clears the current input line; during command execution ^C
  interrupts the in-flight job and returns to the shell prompt

Server / networking (P3-13)
- multi-device LAN server/client over hosted POSIX TCP; server-bridge relay for WSL;
  net_iface IPv4/IPv6; Linux P4 Wi-Fi driver backend; security fixes (shell-escape SSID,
  sparse file-transfer chunks); net_sock_native brace fix; ARM net_file_delivery.h prototypes
VER_END

RELEASE_DATE=2026-06-16
